Chapter: FileSystem
  cites Foreword chapter Path

 The FileSystem effect provides open-file, read-all, close-file, read-file, and write-file.
 To open-file gives a linear FileHandle for the named path.
 To read-all gives the full contents and an updated FileHandle as a Pair.
 To close-file consumes a linear FileHandle.
 To read-file gives the full text contents of the named path.
 To write-file writes text to the named path.

 We say:

Section: Definitions

  effect FileSystem where
    open-file  : Text -> [FileSystem.Read] linear FileHandle
    read-all   : linear FileHandle -> [FileSystem.Read] Pair Text (linear FileHandle)
    close-file : linear FileHandle -> [FileSystem.Write] Nothing
    read-file  : Text -> [FileSystem.Read] Text
    write-file : Text, Text -> [FileSystem.Write] Nothing

Section: Path Utilities

  fs-read-file : Text, Text -> [FileSystem.Read] Text
  fs-read-file (dir) (filename) = read-file (path-join dir filename)

  fs-write-file : Text, Text, Text -> [FileSystem.Write] Nothing
  fs-write-file (dir) (filename) (content) = write-file (path-join dir filename) content

  fs-sibling : Text, Text -> Text
  fs-sibling (filepath) (new-name) = path-join (path-parent filepath) new-name

  fs-with-extension : Text, Text -> Text
  fs-with-extension (filepath) (ext) =
    let base = path-join (path-parent filepath) (path-stem filepath)
    in base & "." & ext

